// The same arithmetic as arith.noe, with nothing in the loop to stop tier 1 compiling it — so
// this row runs on NATIVE code and `arith.noe` runs on the interpreter, and the pair covers both
// engines from a single binary.
//
// Its instruction count carries a deliberately coarse tolerance (see scripts/perf-ratchet.sh):
// tier 1 compiles on a background thread, so how many iterations run interpreted before native
// code is installed depends on machine load — measured, the FLOOR itself moves ~1.2% between an
// idle box and a loaded one. The precise guard on this row is not the number but the assertion
// that it is native at all (`tier1=native`).
mut total = 0
mut i = 0
while i < 10000000 {
    total = total + (i % 7)
    i = i + 1
}
echo total
